    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] Fixture fx_lurob @100b6fbb6e: Payment.order = ForeignKey(Order, related_name='payments'); self.order.mark_paid() -> external:mark_paid with inherited_field_receiver='order' (a class-body field is not an own __init__ field, so Site-3 treats it as inherited and the linker finds nothing); control self.order.payments.create() -> django.db.models:create. relation_fields is still filled at py.py ~5605 and read only via the oracle. Since filing, WI-zamud added a third map (instance_field_types), so 'one fact, one home' now spans three maps. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFiled 2026-09-07 from WI-gulaz. That PR reads a Django model's forward `ForeignKey` / `OneToOneField` class-body fields into `DjangoRelationIndex.relation_fields` (`Payment.order -> Order`) and consults them ONLY through the manager oracle (`self.order.payments`, `payment.order.event.items`). The same fact belongs in the project class field map (`class_field_types[C][field] -> Symbol`) that WI-hiziz Site 3 resolves `self.<field>.<method>()` against -- `self.order.mark_paid()` would then resolve to `Order.mark_paid`, a call-graph edge that today is an unresolved external `mark_paid`. Kept out of WI-gulaz so that PR's measurement priced one mechanism (manager typing) and not two (manager typing + a call-graph resolution change with its own precision profile).\n\nThe 2026-09-06 derivability census sized this as S4 \"Django relation field -> model\": 131 pretix sites, payoff cell \"project class -> no module (precision)\".\n\nWHAT TO BUILD. Feed `relation_fields` into `_collect_class_field_maps`'s output for model classes (the by-class-id maps in `analyze_python`'s pre-pass), gated by the same WI-supat trust rules the constructor-typed fields use. Measure the call-graph delta (resolved edges added, and whether any resolves to the wrong same-short-name class) and the taint delta separately.\n\nONE FACT, ONE HOME: when this lands, `relation_fields` should be read FROM the field map rather than kept as a second map, or the two will drift."  # a9d8
